[{"sha":"566f89e0fb2aa4b2f1ebf98761e45e62aa5ef225","node_id":"C_kwDODihR8toAKDU2NmY4OWUwZmIyYWE0YjJmMWViZjk4NzYxZTQ1ZTYyYWE1ZWYyMjU","commit":{"author":{"name":"Mike Jensen","email":"jentfoo@users.noreply.github.com","date":"2026-10-25T00:39:53Z"},"committer":{"name":"GitHub","email":"noreply@github.com","date":"2026-10-25T00:39:53Z"},"message":"ipn/ipnlocal: fix serve app caps leaking across mounts (#21931)\n\n`serveWebHandler` wrote each mount's accepted app capabilities into the connection-scoped serveHTTPContext. Concurrent h2 streams of one TLS serve connection share that struct, so a request to a mount accepting no capabilities could be proxied carrying another mount's `Tailscale-App-Capabilities` header, letting backends that trust the header authorize the wrong mount.\n\nThis change fixes that issue by storing accepted capabilities per-request via a context value instead of a field on the shared struct.\n\nUpdates tailscale/corp#50380\n\nChange-Id: I5d0a4a02266018f342ba75a1b3291176738ce05b\n\nSigned-off-by: Mike Jensen <mikej@tailscale.com>","tree":{"sha":"8324b9c106e6edf84e0177a23d4d16766075c9b0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tailscale/tailscale/git/trees/8324b9c106e6edf84e0177a23d4d16766075c9b0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tailscale/tailscale/git/commits/566f89e0fb2aa4b2f1ebf98761e45e62aa5ef225","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":true,"reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJq3U/ZCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAbykQAIq0EbGJtkqRxs9HpFtkC4ii\nvtOyB5QwaPI/PMK4kN6s1FPPOzu9B8LibI9QFGIw9mPCFYCH4kDLkBrLlFAcZ1Qq\nc1A4eYlgo0NalU8ZGHjsrVjUd3dUIV8cStSmnEvRQPhsykIo2vO56jW/HpeEzzFh\nYu1pEmh5zMsP4A92S/LCcYankYl+HOPbAjXlZmgw/cBKWr+SYyVmbXgqFMGui7bR\nMRhSgaDsABn5UugZoNhBu2jjb93DrAKSQ+d3kCBMddArNXHcwdadLS6hjCZA3z8A\nxNDbhCldXdDSx/YHL1m2ZRBp8x9tYI9lzE5NvP28gYhI9w488MMKdkDFSVZVwcEG\n4BUzmOMizXsOb7WU1dXLpeZBAdEgxj2WejYNmf6eTo7i/jC86dULMUFP+XH92Ero\nTic1mIsIgjTVLIUc3J6xcEe9kJx0Rv3Tug+9wdpLXAdIIzyNrDTZO6YnnyGEUAxv\n3a9Xd0wpdXFU6vZeTqAuvy/EDzOXyeRBI+AwbBtgT2yO6dcYs22GJJrmYcP/MKWE\nIeiCq2GB7VdJDvJaxxwub56+Luslmg18uDV3e0cm6Q85Im3LwVG+PI5XDtbokZLf\n5A2iMTDpVPvED+El2pLlppCLFQeGRZlJWpFqlvMKA0enjpd+b8GQpqIlenRwRp5n\nRk1iL5hJ1PFlCcUY0TwU\n=9cqy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","payload":"tree 8324b9c106e6edf84e0177a23d4d16766075c9b0\nparent 729cd431b3b40781d342a92a42518b2ba3ff135f\nauthor Mike Jensen <jentfoo@users.noreply.github.com> 1792888793 -0600\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1792888793 -0600\n\nipn/ipnlocal: fix serve app caps leaking across mounts (#21931)\n\n`serveWebHandler` wrote each mount's accepted app capabilities into the connection-scoped serveHTTPContext. Concurrent h2 streams of one TLS serve connection share that struct, so a request to a mount accepting no capabilities could be proxied carrying another mount's `Tailscale-App-Capabilities` header, letting backends that trust the header authorize the wrong mount.\n\nThis change fixes that issue by storing accepted capabilities per-request via a context value instead of a field on the shared struct.\n\nUpdates tailscale/corp#50380\n\nChange-Id: I5d0a4a02266018f342ba75a1b3291176738ce05b\n\nSigned-off-by: Mike Jensen <mikej@tailscale.com>","verified_at":"2026-10-25T00:39:53Z"}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tailscale/tailscale/commits/566f89e0fb2aa4b2f1ebf98761e45e62aa5ef225","html_url":"https://github.com/tailscale/tailscale/commit/566f89e0fb2aa4b2f1ebf98761e45e62aa5ef225","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tailscale/tailscale/commits/566f89e0fb2aa4b2f1ebf98761e45e62aa5ef225/comments","author":{"login":"jentfoo","id":2165757,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxNjU3NTc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2165757?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jentfoo","html_url":"https://github.com/jentfoo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jentfoo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jentfoo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jentfoo